    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0658" n="554" xml:id="pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4688: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-10T22:00:00+01:00">March 10, 1932—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 10—6:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. Supplementing my 69, March 10, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="82" xml:id="d598-f1"/>
                    apparently reference to the Kellogg Pact was omitted in the
                    final paragraph of part I of the text of the resolution for the reason that the
                    point was raised that certain members of the League of Nations were not
                    signatories to the Kellogg Pact. However, this question is
                    being agitated tonight and discussion is taking place as to whether it will not
                    be possible to insert a final phrase reading somewhat as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“or in so far as concerns signatories of the Pact of Paris by means
                            contrary to that Pact”.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d598-f1" n="82" xml:id="d598-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted text of draft Assembly resolution. For text as
                    adopted March 11, see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_210"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 210</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
